# OBOROZUKI MANOR 1F -- Genkan & Great Hall   (14x10, TILESET_TRADITIONAL_HOUSE, ref DanceTheater)
# Story: the Oborozuki ("hazy moon") family have kept Ecruteak's Kimono Girls for generations and
# host the seasonal moon-viewing dance. The head, Lady Sayo (retired tea grandmaster, once a Kimono
# Girl), shut herself in the family's Moon Shrine during the last eclipse and has not come out.
# Layout: earth genkan along the bottom (front door mats bottom-centre), wooden hallway up the middle,
# tea room on the left behind a wooden screen, waiting nook on the right, reception hall across the
# top with tokonoma scrolls (14) and shoji windows (2d), sliding-door track line (0d) under it.
# Gameplay: the stairs block (13,1) is reachable from two sides, so one NPC cannot block it: use coord
# events on (26,2) and (27,3) that make the Steward stop you until the tea ceremony is done.
# PUZZLE (tea room): serve the four guests on the long-table cushions in the order of the four
# seasons, STARTING FROM THE CURRENT SEASON (wSeason) -- the hanging scroll gives the poem order.
# Needs the TEA CADDY from the Kura. Wrong order = the guest leaves, try again.
# Warps: FRONT mats (13,19)(14,19) -> estate grounds front door. EAST carpet (27,12)(27,13) ->
# Engawa mats. STAIRS 39 (27,2) -> Study 2F stairs (3,3).
tileset traditional_house
ref DanceTheater
